<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paras Ram</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">17th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paras Ram was a member of the Umat Parmar ruling house of Rajgarh in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a>, central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, who founded the state of Narsinghgarh in 1681. He separated part of the family lands to form his own state, with the town of Narsinghgarh as its seat. His descendants ruled Narsinghgarh as a princely state under British paramountcy until 1948.</p></div>
